## 3. Walkthrough & Exam Drills

### Drill 1: Deploy Storage Provisioner (`01-provisioners/`)

Dynamic volume provisioning in Kubernetes requires an active storage controller or Container Storage Interface (CSI)
provisioner plugin. The provisioner watches for new `PersistentVolumeClaim` objects that request its `StorageClass`,
dynamically provisions the backing storage, and automatically generates matching `PersistentVolume` resources.

#### Step 1: Deploy Local Path Provisioner

Deploy the Rancher `local-path-provisioner`, which provisions host-based storage directories on the cluster worker
nodes:

```bash
cd {{ cka_lab_storage_classes_dir }}/01-provisioners

./install-local-path-provisioner.sh
kubectl get pods -n local-path-storage
```

Verify that the provisioner pod is `Running`. It registers the `rancher.io/local-path` provisioner plugin with the
Kubernetes API server.

